// What people do for a living.
//
// Each trade names the social class whose wages and politics it shares, so the market did
// not have to be rewritten to gain a population screen: nine professions map onto the four
// classes the economy already priced.
//
// The two shares are the same trade in two different places. A farming region is mostly
// peasants; a city is mostly wage labour, counters and desks. Rather than author a profile
// for every country, each trade says what it is worth in the countryside and what it is
// worth in a city, and a region blends the two by how urban it actually is - so
// Bangladesh and Belgium end up with different populations without either being written down.
//
// Shares are weights, not percentages: they are normalised per region, so a mod may add a
// tenth profession without having to rebalance the other nine.
